---
import { DESKTOP_DOWNLOADS, DESKTOP_RELEASES_URL } from "../lib/links";

const systems = [
  { name: "macOS, Apple Silicon (M1 and later)", files: [{ url: DESKTOP_DOWNLOADS.macArm64, type: ".dmg" }] },
  { name: "macOS, Intel", files: [{ url: DESKTOP_DOWNLOADS.macX64, type: ".dmg" }] },
  { name: "Windows", files: [{ url: DESKTOP_DOWNLOADS.winX64, type: ".exe" }] },
  {
    name: "Linux",
    files: [
      { url: DESKTOP_DOWNLOADS.linuxAppImage, type: ".AppImage" },
      { url: DESKTOP_DOWNLOADS.linuxDeb, type: ".deb", note: "Debian, Ubuntu" },
    ],
  },
];
---

<section id="download" class="border-t border-line">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Also on your desktop</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-muted">
      The same workspace as the web app, from import to G-code, for macOS, Windows and Linux. No
      account and no internet connection needed: projects are <code>.furrow</code> files on your
      computer, with their saved versions, and open in the web app too. Free and MIT-licensed.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-px border border-line bg-line sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        systems.map((s) => (
          <li class="bg-bg p-4">
            {s.name}
            {s.files.map((f) => (
              <a href={f.url} class="mt-2 block break-all text-xs text-muted underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-fg">
                {f.type}
                {f.note && ` (${f.note})`}
              </a>
            ))}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-6 text-muted">
      Release notes and older versions are on the{" "}
      <a href={DESKTOP_RELEASES_URL} class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-fg">releases page</a>.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-12 font-semibold">First launch</h3>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-muted">
      The installers aren't code-signed yet, so your system warns you the first time you open the
      app.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-6 max-w-2xl space-y-3">
      <li>
        <span class="text-muted">→</span> <strong class="font-semibold">macOS:</strong> open System
        Settings → Privacy &amp; Security, scroll down to the message about Furrow CAM and click{" "}
        <strong class="font-semibold">Open Anyway</strong>, then confirm.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-muted">→</span> <strong class="font-semibold">Windows:</strong> when
        SmartScreen shows "Windows protected your PC", click{" "}
        <strong class="font-semibold">More info</strong>, then{" "}
        <strong class="font-semibold">Run anyway</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-muted">→</span> <strong class="font-semibold">Linux:</strong> make the
        AppImage executable (<code>chmod +x</code>) and run it, or install the <code>.deb</code> with{" "}
        <code>sudo apt install ./furrow-cam-*.deb</code>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-muted">
      There's no automatic update yet: download new versions from this page.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
